 "text": "Perry County, Ohio | Treasurer\nSkip to Content Skip to navigation\nPerry County, Ohio\nToggle navigation\nServices +\n911\nAuditor\nBoard of Developmental Disabilities\nBoard of Elections\nBureau of Motor Vehicles\nCommissioners\nCoroner\nDistrict Library\nDog Shelter\nEmergency Management\nEngineer\nFairview Assisted Living\nHealth Department\nJob & Family Services\nLand Bank\nMobility Management\nOSU Extension Office\nPark District\nSenior Center\nSoil & Water Conservation\nTourism & Lodging Tax\nTransit\nTreasurer\nVeterans Services Commission\nWaste Reduction & Recycling\nWater & Wastewater\nRecords +\nPublic Notices\nClerk of Courts\nRecorder\nTitle Office\nLaw & Courts +\nCommon Pleas\nMunicipal Court\nProbate & Juvenile\nProsecutor\nSheriff’s Office\nPeople +\nDirectory\nJob Opportunities\nHuman Resources\nEvents\nHome About News\nNow: 1792341271 - October 18, 2026, 16:34:31 (GMT)\nStart: 1766725200 - December 26, 2025, 05:00:00 (GMT)\nEnd: 1792341271 - October 18, 2026, 16:34:31 (GMT)\nTreasurer\nI want to...\nPay My Water Bill\nPurchase / Renew a Dog License\nGet / Renew a Driver’s License\nContact Children Services\nContact My Commissioners\nReport a Crime\nI need a record...\nVehicle, Boat Titles\nTax Records\nProperty Records\nCourt Records\nCrime Incident Records\nI need assistance...\nPublic Safety Issue\nChild Safety Situation\nElderly Safety Situation\nFood or Housing\nSubstance or Addiction Issues\nAgricultural Issues\nTax Issues\nTREASURER\nTheresa Moore\nOFFICE LOCATION\n212 S. Main Street, Upper Level\nNew Lexington, Ohio 43764\nMAILING ADDRESS\nP.O. Box 288\nNew Lexington, OH 43764\nHOURS OF OPERATION\nMonday – Friday\n8:00 am – 4:00 pm\nClosed on Federal holidays.\nOffice Phone (740) 342-1235 or (740) 721-0118\nFax (740) 342-4710\nVisit Website\nSEND EMAIL\nPerry County Treasurer\nNOTICE: The due date for property taxes has been extended to August 21, 2026.\nAs your Perry County Treasurer , my duties include serving as the county’s chief investment officer, managing delinquent tax collections and safeguarding the property tax escrow account. I also serve as county banker, custodian of all taxes and investor of local funds.\nThe goal of my staff and I is to provide the best possible service to the residents of Perry County.\nAt the Perry County Treasurer’s office, we look forward to serving you. If you have any questions or require further information, please do not hesitate to call our office at (740) 342-1235 or email us .\nFREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS\nWhen are taxes due?\nThe second half property taxes has been extended to August 21, 2026.\nWhat is the penalty if I pay my taxes late?\nFor the first 10 days after the due date, there is a 5% penalty. After 10 days past due, it’s 10%.\nMy name is on the unclaimed funds list on your website. How do I claim this?\nClick the button below, complete the claim form to print and mail in with appropriate ID and paperwork as described on the claim form.\nFILE TO CLAIM FUNDS\nPerry County, Ohio\nAbout\nVillages, Townships & Communities\nDiscover Perry County\nPerry County Photos\nRecords\nClerk of Courts\nRecorder\nTitle Office\nNews\nEvents\nFair Housing Information\nDepartments & Offices\n911\nAuditor\nBoard of Developmental Disabilities\nBoard of Elections\nBureau of Motor Vehicles\nCommissioners\nCoroner\nDog Shelter\nEmergency Management\nEngineer\nFairview Assisted Living\nHealth Department\nJob & Family Services\nLand Bank\nPark District\nMobility Management\nOSU Extension\nSenior Center\nSoil & Water Conservation\nTourism\nTransit\nTreasurer\nVeterans Services Commission\nWaste & Recycling\nWater & Wastewater\nLaw & Courts\nCommon Pleas\nJuvenile/Probate\nMulti-County Juvenile Facility\nMunicipal\nProsecutor\nSheriff\nPeople\nDirectory\nJob Opportunities\nHuman Resources\n212 S. Main Street, New Lexington, OH 43764 • (740) 342-2045\n© Copyright 2026 Perry County, All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy • Website Accessibility Statement • Site Map",
